# Bread Pudding

Based on [https://www.allrecipes.com/…](https://www.allrecipes.com/recipe/7177/bread-pudding-ii) ([wayback](http://web.archive.org/web/20251123145513/https://www.allrecipes.com/recipe/7177/bread-pudding-ii))

{ rating="5" image="bread_pudding.jpeg" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

- [ ] 1/2 Baguette or [other stale bread]{ ing="other-stale-bread" }, small pieces
- [ ] 2 Tbsp [butter]{ ing="butter" }, melted
- [ ] 2 cups [milk]{ ing="milk" }
- [ ] 3/4 cup [sugar]{ ing="sugar" }
- [ ] 4 [eggs]{ ing="egg" }, beaten
- [ ] 1.5 tsp [cinnamon]{ ing="cinnamon" }
- [ ] 1 tsp [vanilla]{ ing="vanilla" }

## Recipe

1. Preheat oven to 350F
1. In 8” square pan, place [bread]{ ing="other-stale-bread" } scraps and sprinkle [butter]{ ing="butter" } over top
1. In a large mixing bowl, whisk [milk]{ ing="milk" }, [sugar]{ ing="sugar" }, [eggs]{ ing="egg" }, [cinnamon]{ ing="cinnamon" }, and [vanilla]{ ing="vanilla" } until well combined
1. Pour in the mixture and use a fork to make sure the bread is submerged
1. Bake until golden brown and the top springs back, about 45 min

## Notes

- Goes great with Horchata Ice Cream!
- _Consider chocolate variations, adding chocolate chips or nutella for serving, etc._
